Add-on Store client - third-party licenses\par
\par
The client's own code is licensed under the MIT License (the repository's LICENSE; the setup shows it above this text). It contains two third-party components:\par
\par
- Microsoft WebView2 SDK 1.0.4258.31, static loader (WebView2LoaderStatic.lib, linked into PluginStore.zxt), BSD-3-Clause, https://www.nuget.org/packages/Microsoft.Web.WebView2. The WebView2 runtime itself is part of Windows and is not shipped with the client.\par
- Red Hat Display (font) 1.023, Light, Regular, Medium and Bold, embedded unchanged in the store window page inside PluginStore.zxt (since 1.9.18), SIL Open Font License 1.1, https://github.com/RedHatOfficial/RedHatFont.\par
\par
The installer (MSI) is built with the WiX Toolset 3.14; it contains no WiX runtime parts (no WiX dialogs, bitmaps, texts or custom action DLLs). Its dialogs, texts and banner are our own.\par
\par
Tungsten Automation's own parts (not third-party, listed for completeness):\par
\par
- Tungsten Plug-in UI kit 1.1.0 (styles and scripts inlined into the store window page), MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Tungsten Automation.\par
- Tungsten Power PDF Plugin SDK 2025.3.6: the plug-in entry file pimain.cpp (unchanged SDK source) is compiled into PluginStore.zxt, Copyright Tungsten Automation; it is not covered by the MIT License of the client's own code.\par
- Tungsten Automation logo 2026 and the Power PDF symbol, property of Tungsten Automation, used per the Brand Book.\par
\par
Microsoft Visual C++: PluginStore.zxt uses the MFC and C++ runtime DLLs that Power PDF itself requires and ships none of them; AddonStoreLink.exe links the Visual C++ runtime statically (Visual Studio license terms), so no runtime DLL is part of the MSI.\par
